PC Utility

HIGHLIGHTS

o  One monthly service fee for a complete multivendor desktop solution,
   including systems, software, networking, and total support

o  Helps users control the hidden, escalating costs of PC ownership

o  Enables users to maintain a competitive edge by focusing on core business
   competencies

SERVICE DESCRIPTION

PC Utility is a unique offer designed to relieve the costs and
administrative headaches of PC ownership. For one monthly service fee per
desktop, users receive a complete portfolio of desktop services. Core
services include program management, software and hardware acquisition,
staging and installation, hardware maintenance, technology refresh and
upgrades, telephone support, software licenses and updates, and project
management. Contracts are customized and may include other Digital services,
depending on user needs. Recommended options are asset management, user
training, and LAN management. Contracts extend for at least three years.

The move to client/server computing and the proliferation of PCs have
created many hidden costs for organizations. According to a 1994 Gartner
Group study, "Management Strategies to Control the Rapidly Escalating Cost
of Ownership," the cost of buying PCs is only 15 percent of the total costs
of owning and managing a PC environment. Budgets and staff time are consumed
by efforts to support, manage, track, and upgrade increasingly complex
environments.

The PC Utility provides a range of desktop services for a single monthly
fee. In addition, users can acquire the client/server solution -- including
equipment -- for a monthly operating expense rather than as a capital cost.
This is a significant financial advantage. PC assets depreciate faster in
the marketplace than on financial books. The comprehensive single service
agreement provides an increased return on investments and assets when
compared with traditional methods of purchasing, supporting, and servicing
desktop products. In addition, users are not locked into one technology that
may become obsolete before it is written off the financial books.

The value of the program is not in each service offered but in the seamless
application of services to solve a business problem. This innovative
solution was recognized by Service News (April 1995), which gave its annual
"Best Service" award to PC Utility.

The PC Utility and the Software Utility (see the "Software Utility" article
in this issue) take a coherent, integrated approach to an entire business
problem, providing a high level of flexibility in meeting user needs. While
the Software Utility focuses on the costs and complexity of managing
software assets, PC Utility addresses all areas associated with desktop
ownership.

BENEFITS

o  Gives users access to the latest client/server technology while reducing
   the burdens of management, support, and maintenance.

o  Users are able to refocus on what they do best -- their core competencies
   -- and thereby increase their competitive advantage.

o  "Pay-as-you-go" service eliminates large cash outlays and capital
   expenditures.

o  Eliminates risk of user's technology becoming obsolete.

o  Gives users one point of contract for acquisition, support, and
   management of their client/server environments.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

PC Utility is available now in the following countries -- U.S., Canada,
Australia, New Zealand, United Kingdom, France, Ireland, Holland, Belgium,
Italy, Spain, Switzerland, Denmark, Finland, Germany, Luxembourg, Sweden,
Austria, and Norway. It will be available in additional countries in the
near future.

Each PC Utility agreement must be customized, though there is a standard
contract for terms and conditions. There is no PC Utility part number.

