Software Utility

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Delivers complete management capabilities at every stage of the software
   life cycle

o  Provides an effective way to reduce both the direct and the indirect
   costs of software ownership

o  Frees staff from manual tasks

o  Delivers essential capabilities for the implementation and management of
   client/server environments

SERVICE DESCRIPTION

The Software Utility service has two primary goals: to reduce costs wherever
possible in the user's environment and to restore management and control in
multivendor environments, many of which have seen an uncontrolled
proliferation of software products over the past few years. It delivers
complete management capabilities at every stage of the software life cycle
-- from product evaluation and selection to acquisition, distribution,
installation, license tracking, and ongoing technical support. The Software
Utility is composed of four major components:

o  Software product -- Digital tracks and reports volume purchases of
   software for large worldwide companies, allowing these organizations to
   qualify for larger discounts.

o  Software management -- Digital offers services that include Asset
   Management Consulting, a comprehensive, onsite evaluation of current
   management processes. The results of the evaluation and the
   characteristics of the user's environment determine which services and
   tools should be included in the overall solution.

o  Design and implementation services -- Digital provides users with the
   tools and training they need to set up and maintain a comprehensive asset
   management program for hardware and software. Among the asset management
   tools available is POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software. This product, a
   recipient of two industry awards, extends Microsoft System Manager
   capabilities for PCs to OpenVMS software and the most popular UNIX
   platforms, including those from Hewlett Packard, IBM, and Sun. AssetWORKS
   software manages hardware and software inventories, electronic software
   distribution and installation, and reporting for enterprisewide
   applications in mixed PC and non-PC environments.

o  Support services for end users and technical staff -- The Software
   Utility, combined with the PC Utility (see the "PC Utility" article in
   this issue), provides a complete acquisition, support, and management
   solution for multivendor hardware and software environments.

The Software Utility and PC Utility represent a highly effective response to
recent marketplace trends. By taking a coherent, integrated approach to an
entire business problem, and providing for a high level of flexibility in
the implementation of a comprehensive solution, these programs allow Digital
to meet clearly identified user needs more easily and predictably. While the
PC Utility addresses the costs and complexity of overall desktop ownership,
the Software Utility focuses on the key area of software management:
addressing software cost of ownership, which is exploding in most large
companies. This includes direct expenses for acquisition, which represent 24
percent of total software costs, plus the indirect or "hidden" costs
involved in the other stages of the software life cycle, which make up the
other 76 percent.

BENEFITS

o  Offers comprehensive and flexible management capabilities that are
   designed specifically to meet today's software asset management
   challenges.

o  Delivers cost savings in several key areas, including license,
   administrative, and distribution costs.

o  Provides the electronic capabilities essential to the implementation of
   client/server computing, which requires a high degree of synchronization
   between updates on client/server applications. A change to the back end
   of an application could require updating thousands of PCs in a few hours.
   This cannot be achieved without the use of industrial strength tools for
   the electronic distribution and installation of software.

o  Enhances accountability and responsiveness by allowing the user to work
   with a single partner for all popular PC software, applications, and
   support.

o  Provides worldwide capabilities, allowing major international enterprises
   to standardize control and savings throughout their operations.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Software Utility is available now on a custom quote basis worldwide from
Digital.



