StorageWorks HSZ40 Array Controller for Fast, Wide Differential SCSI-2

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides more than 50 percent improved controller and adapter I/O
   performance and connection for up to 42 SCSI devices

o  Utilizes StorageWorks BA350-Mx shelf with room for dual-redundant
   HSZ40-Bx controllers, eliminating single point of failure

o  Offers dramatically lower, more competitive pricing, including a 15
   percent savings for a fully configured system

o  Replaces HSZ40-Ax controller

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The StorageWorks HSZ40-Bx Array Controller brings improved SCSI-2
performance to the StorageWorks family of controller products. When used in
combination with the new KZPSA PCI-SCSI adapter, the HSZ40-Bx provides up to
2,100 I/O requests per second and 13.6 MB per second of bandwidth.

The inclusion of 16 or 32 MB of read and write-back cache provides excellent
response times. Write-back cache, which improves performance during write
operations, is required to utilize disk mirroring and parity RAID
StorageSets. Disk mirroring is a new optional feature of the HS Operating
Firmware V2.5 firmware. (See the "StorageWorks HS Operating Firmware V2.5
with Optional Disk Mirroring" article in this issue.)

The array controller connects to a host computer system using a fast, wide
differential SCSI-2 bus. Up to four SCSI target addresses are supported by
either single or dual-redundant controller configurations. Dual-redundant
controllers can be configured for high availability. This allows support for
up to 32 SCSI logical units for a dual-redundant HSZ40 Array Controller
configuration.

Users can purchase the fully configured HSZ40-BF option (with 32 MB read and
write-back cache, RAID, and disk mirroring). Alternatively, write-back cache
with standard battery backup can be purchased as an upgrade from read cache,
with RAID and disk mirroring available as separate options.

The HSZ40-Bx SCSI Array Controller will replace the HSZ40-Ax SCSI Array
Controller, while providing high availability, higher performance, and
competitive pricing. The HSZ40-Ax will no longer be available after August
1995.

BENEFITS

o  High performance
   - HSZ40-Bx and KZPSA provide up to 2,100 I/O requests per second and 13.6
     MB per second of bandwidth, increasing application performance.
   - Provides controller-based RAID 0 (striping).
   - Up to 32 MB of optional read and write-back cache (with battery backup
     unit for data protection).

o  High availability
   - Optional controller-based disk mirroring offloads host-based shadowing
     for improved ease of management and lower system I/O bus traffic.
   - Dual-redundant HSZ40 support with Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1)
     V3.2 supporting high availability system configurations.
   - Controller warm swap provides ability to replace devices without taking
     system down.

o  Connectivity for storage expansion and availability
   - A single HSZ40 controller supports 42 single SCSI devices or 36 devices
   in dual-redundant configurations.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

HSZ40-Bx Array Controllers are available now.

Prerequisites for disk mirroring option are write-back cache (HSZ40-YX) and
HS Operating Firmware V2.5 firmware. HS Operating Firmware V2.5 is not
available for HSZ40-Ax at this time, but is planned for the near future. HS
Operating Firmware V2.5 will be the last release of firmware to support the
HSZ40-Ax controllers. Dual redundancy is not possible using an HSZ40-Bx and
HSC40-Ax.

