StorageWorks HS Operating Firmware V2.5 with Optional Disk Mirroring

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Disk mirroring option for StorageWorks HSD, HSJ, and HSZ Array
   Controllers for highly available data protection

o  Improved I/O performance on HSZ40 and HSD30 controller and adapter
   combinations

o  Improved disk and tape support

o  30 percent price reduction on existing HS Operating Firmware RAID option

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

With StorageWorks HS Operating Firmware V2.5, Digital has built upon the
device connectivity, I/O processing, and write-back cache capabilities of
the HS series of array controllers in creating a subsystem-based mirrored
disk option. The disk mirroring option is a robust, highly functional,
second generation implementation of Digital's disk mirroring technology.

V2.5 also provides expanded features, device connectivity, and performance
to assure high availability and ease of system management. New features
include improved performance in disk copy data and HSZ40 failover. HS
Operating Firmware V2.5 supports increased performance on the HSD30, from
1,000 to 1,150 I/O requests per second, and on the HSZ40-Bx, from 1,350 to
2,050 I/O requests per second.

HS Operating Firmware V2.5 provides multi-lun support on the TZ867 with
Storage Library System V2.5b. This allows tapes on the TZ867 to be randomly
accessed, optomizing archival operations. Additionally, failover of
dual-redundant HSZ40 array controllers is now supported with Digital UNIX
(formerly called DEC OSF/1) V3.2 for improved data availability.

Disk Mirroring Option

The HS Operating Firmware V2.5 Disk Mirroring option includes the following
capabilities:

o  The option includes from two to six identical copies of data on
   mirrorsets. Mirrorsets may be utilized under disksets or stripeset units
   attached to a single StorageWorks HSx Array Controller for availability
   and performance enhancement.

o  It utilizes the StorageWorks Write-back Cache option for HSx array
   controllers, minimizing the impact of multiple member writes on
   application responsiveness while protecting mirrorset integrity.

o  When utilized in conjunction with dual-redundant HSx controller
   configurations, it provides protection against controller and disk
   failures.

o  Mirrorsets may be striped for high performance access to large amounts of
   highly available data.

o  The option includes the automatic replacement of a failed mirrorset
   member with a spare disk as well as the versatility to include multiple
   disk types in a single mirror set.

o  For ease of backup, disk mirroring may be used to obtain snapshot copies
   of data on striped and mirrored data (not applicable to RAID data).

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

StorageWorks HS Operating Firmware V2.5 for HSJ30/40, HSD30, and HSZ40-Bx is
available now. HS Operating Firmware V2.5 for HSZ40-Ax will be available
June 15, 1995.

Letters or faxes announcing the new capabilities supported by V2.5 will be
sent to all users who have registered for warranty on the HS series of
controllers. The letters will include a form to be completed and returned to
register for the warranty and to ensure shipment of the new firmware
release.

Users who wish to continue to receive warranty and MDDS distribution of HS
Operating Firmware must return the PCMCIA card containing a previous HS
Operating Firmware release after verifying proper operation of the new one.
A pre-paid, pre-addressed mailer is provided with every firmware upgrade.

Ordering the Write-back Cache Option

Some early HSJ40 controllers will need new cache modules to be able to
implement write-back cache. Digital will upgrade early version cache at no
extra charge. Users should use the controller command, "SHOW
THIS_CONTROLLER" to see which cache version they have. Version 1 cache
modules must be upgraded; version 2 modules are ready for the write-back
cache option. Options include license, key, and battery. Users who need the
upgrade should use the order numbers HSJ40-YA (16 MB) and HSJ40-YB (32 MB)
when they require the upgrade to version 2 cache.

To obtain cache for controllers bought without cache, users need to order
the read cache options based upon controller type -- HSxxx-XD to receive a
16 MB read cache, or HSxxx-XF to obtain a 32 MB read cache. Users also need
to order the appropriate write-back cache option to receive the battery,
license, and software key to activate write-back cache.

To add more cache to controllers with 16 MB cache, users should order
HSxxx-XE to obtain a 32 MB cache module (requires return of 16 MB cache), as
