AlphaServer 1000 4/233 Pedestal, Rackmount, and Cabinet Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides outstanding value for deploying client/server applications

o  Ideal workgroup server for PC LAN consolidation, Internet access,
   database, or other business critical applications

o  Offers leadership price/performance, expandability, and value, backed by
   the industry's best warranty, to commercial and technical computing users

o  Affordable, high availability solutions through clustering

o  Delivers expanded storage, I/O, and in-cabinet systems integration
   capabilities (rackmount and cabinet versions)

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Pedestal System

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 system is a 233 MHz Alpha uniprocessor server in
a deskside tower enclosure running Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1),
OpenVMS, or Windows NT software. It replaces the AlphaServer 1000 4/200 at
the same price, and offers high reliability features, such as fully
redundant power supplies, internal RAID, hot swap disks, a dual SCSI
backplane, ECC memory, and ECC cache.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 provides for up to 10 internal mass storage
devices, which include a floppy diskette drive and a CD-ROM. The server also
supports up to 512 MB of RAM, up to 7 hot swap StorageWorks disk drives, and
a tape drive, and will soon support wide SCSI devices. Over 28 GB of
internal disk storage will be possible with the new 4.3 GB disk drive, the
fastest 4 GB drive on the market, running at 7,200 RPM. PCI-based FDDI, RAID
controllers, and asynchronous multiplexers also are supported on the new
AlphaServer 1000 4/233. All this expandability, using PC industry-standard
components such as 72-pin 36 bit SIMMs, provides balanced system performance
at an affordable price.

The following items are integrated on the system motherboard:

o  Industry standard SVGA controller
o  Floppy disk controller
o  Two serial ports and one parallel port
o  Keyboard and mouse controller
o  LCD operator control panel
o  PCI-based fast SCSI-2 controller

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 offers server management features, such as heat,
fan failure, and power supply sensors. Remote management can be handled via
a simple serial link. The system includes an LCD operator control panel.

The reliability features, combined with simple management features, make the
AlphaServer 1000 ideal for organizations with little or no MIS support.
Business critical applications can run unattended, as management features
provide early indications of potential system failures.

Remote diagnosis allows resellers and system administrators to call in and
remotely run the diagnostics, configure the system, recommend a fix, or pull
the right part. Support costs are minimized because onsite visits and
service calls are minimized.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 was designed to offer investment protection
through easy system upgrades to faster processors. High availability, high
performance, and linear expandability also are offered through Digital's
unique clustering technology, including DECsafe Available Server for Digital
UNIX systems. The new system will also support OpenVMS SCSI clusters when
they become available.

Rackmount and Cabinet Systems

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 Rackmount server systems offer functionality
identical to the AlphaServer 1000 4/233 pedestal systems by utilizing the
same CPU, memory, power supply, and I/O. When integrated in 19-inch
industry-standard cabinets, the small workgroup servers take on
unprecedented price/performance leadership.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 Rackmount offers two PCI slots, seven EISA bus
master slots, and one PCI/EISA interleaved slot in the rackmount tower
enclosure. The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 Rackmount provides support for up to
five mass storage devices, which include a floppy diskette drive and CD-ROM.
The rackmounted server systems support up to 512 MB of RAM memory and 6 GB
of internal system disk storage. Additional storage is available through the
use of rackmounted StorageWorks shelves.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 Rackmount and Cabinet systems are available in
packaged systems as well as system building blocks for flexibility in
meeting users' unique configuration needs. These systems can be purchased
separately without a cabinet enclosure or purchased as a cabinet
configuration that includes the AlphaServer 1000 4/233 integrated into an
H9A10-C* enclosure.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 Pedestal, Rackmount, and Cabinet systems are
available now. More details on CPU upgrades and ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES will be
available in a future Digital's Customer Update article. Supplemental
service part numbers listed are U.S. only.

