AdvantageCluster File Server 5004/275 for Networked File Server Applications

HIGHLIGHTS

o  AdvantageCluster File Server 5004/275 systems are based on AlphaServer
   2100 4/275 systems and the GIGAswitch product, and are scalable to
   deliver the industry's highest Networked File System (NFS) throughput

o  AdvantageCluster File Server systems are built to provide outstanding NFS
   performance while handling an extremely high volume of NFS requests

o  AdvantageCluster File Server systems are packaged with POLYCENTER
   applications for high performance and easy management

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

In today's environment where systems are being overloaded with increasing
amounts of data, users need a flexible system that yields extremely fast
access to files and data. As networks have grown, with workstation upsizing
and mainframe downsizing, the load on systems for file access has also
grown. Users commonly complain about the slow network file server response
time when accessing files and data.

Digital can provide users with a completely scalable Digital UNIX (formerly
DEC OSF/1) based solution to increase the throughput and response time for
NFS requests. The AdvantageCluster File Server 5004/275 rackmounted systems
are scalable to allow users to start small and add CPUs or nodes as their
requirements dictate. The systems are prepackaged with the necessary
hardware and software to yield the most efficient configuration for fast NFS
transactions. Packages include Digital's GIGAswitch product, the industry's
only FDDI crossbar switch offering a 3.6 GB per second bandwidth. The
GIGAswitch product is also ATM-ready, providing users with a smooth
migration to ATM technology.

The AdvantageCluster File Server 5000 systems are designed for users whose
applications require high NFS throughput, such as application development
(CASE) systems in discrete industries (ECAD and MCAD), and high-performance
applications using large data files over networks.

BENEFITS

o  Support for large numbers of users and files over several network
   segments -- The AdvantageCluster File Server 5004/275 can deliver 4,000
   SPECnfs operations per second at a response time of tens of milliseconds.

o  Quick response time to large amounts of data -- Enables information and
   results to be shared more readily across the organization.

o  A single integrated package -- Simplifies the ordering, configuration,
   and start-up, creating an optimal server system.

o  AlphaServer 2100 4/275 rackmounted systems -- Provide industry-leading
   price/performance.

o  The GIGAswitch product offers the fastest FDDI communication rates --
   Increases overall communication between nodes in the cluster, yielding a
   quick response time.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The AdvantageCluster File Server 5004/275 is available now. The system is
custom configurable to meet each user's pricing and performance needs.

