PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Cognos, Inc.'s PowerHouse fourth-generation language (4GL) is a server based
application development tool that allows programmers to work in classic
character-based development environments to build transaction processing,
batch processing, and production reporting applications. PowerHouse software
supports Oracle, SYBASE, and other databases on Digital UNIX based Alpha
systems. Installed at more 8,000 sites worldwide, the product is the
number-one-selling advanced application development language for OpenVMS
based VAX and Alpha systems.

PowerHouse Client software allows users to move into client/server computing
by building and deploying a graphical user interface for their server based
applications and data. Developers can use PowerHouse Client to extend
applications developed on OpenVMS or Digital UNIX systems to the Microsoft
Windows and Macintosh environments. Users can take advantage of PowerHouse
software's support for the Digital UNIX operating system to migrate from
proprietary to open systems, ultimately moving to client/server
architectures.

