___________________________________________________________________________
ULTRIX Remote Installation Services for DEC OSF/1 Clients to be Retired

Remote Installation Services (RIS) software allows users to install DEC
OSF/1 (now called Digital UNIX) software from a central server onto one or
more client workstations. In DEC OSF/1 V3.x, the Remote Installation
Services server could be either an ULTRIX MIPS system or a DEC OSF/1 Alpha
system. After surveying its installed base, Digital determined that no one
is currently using an ULTRIX server to remotely install DEC OSF/1 clients.
Therefore, Digital will retire ULTRIX to DEC OSF/1 Remote Installation
Services software by September 1996. Note that Digital will continue to
support the ability to remotely install ULTRIX clients from an ULTRIX
server, as well as the ability to remotely install DEC OSF/1 clients from a
DEC OSF/1 server.

___________________________________________________________________________
Correction to 4-mm Digital Audio Tape (DAT) Loader Subsystems

Digital's TLZ7L is not supported on rackmount versions of the AlphaServer
2100 4/200 and 4/275, as stated on page 33 of the March 1995 issue of
Customer Update. The TLZ7L loader, as a sequential only device, is supported
under DEC OSF/1 V2.0B, OpenVMS Alpha V6.1, and Windows NT V3.5 on Digital's
AlphaServer 2100 4/200 and 4/275 pedestal server systems.

___________________________________________________________________________
Correction to AlphaServer 8200 5/300 Rackmount Server Availability

We regret that an error regarding the availability of the AlphaServer 8200
5/300 Rackmount Server was made in the April 1995 issue of Sales Update.
Instead of being available for ordering in April, with shipping to begin in
May, the AlphaServer 8200 5/300 Rackmount Server will be available in late
summer.



