RapidPrint 200

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Low cost network interface box for one or two printers

o  Supports multiple protocols: Novell, Apple, LAT, and TCP/IP

o  Easy to install -- standalone or attached to printer

o  Can be easily managed by PConsole (Novell's Management Utility), MOP,
   SNMP, and TSM

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The RapidPrint 200 is a network interface box that directly replaces the
DECserver 250. Unlike the DECserver 250, it supports Alpha and Digital UNIX
(formerly called DEC OSF/1) platforms. It has two ports: one serial and one
parallel. Both ports can be active simultaneously.

The serial port has the following characteristics:

o  Full bidirectional
o  115,000 baud maximum throughput
o  Hardware or XON/XOFF flow control
o  RS423 interface with RJ45 connector

The parallel port (DB25) has the following characteristics:

o  Full bidirectional or unidirectional
o  50,000 bytes per second minimum throughput
o  Can be configured for Centronics, Bitronics, or Dataproducts

Reverse channel or backchannel mode for one printer hook-up allows data to
the printer via the parallel port for high throughput. The data from the
printer is transmitted back to the host via the serial port. This mode is
for printers like the LF02 and DEClaser 1152, which have a unidirectional
parallel port, providing high performance bidirectional communications to
hosts requiring feedback, including VAX systems with DCPS or Macintosh
systems. This feature requires printers that offer the capability to provide
feedback to the serial port while taking in data via the parallel port.

Both 10BaseT and 10Base2 are available. The default is 10Base2, but it can
be changed via a switch.

The following protocols will be active concurrently: Novell, Apple, LAT, and
TCP/IP. The TCP/IP protocol includes LPR/LPD capability. The RapidPrint 200
can be managed via PConsole (Novell's Management Utility), MOP, SNMP, and
TSM.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

The RapidPrint 200 network interface box directly replaces the DECserver
250. It exceeds the throughput requirements of the DECserver 250 and
provides support for newer printers as well as older, installed printer
technology.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The RapidPrint 200 is available now through Digital, the DECdirect service,
and Digital's authorized resellers, value-added resellers, OEMs, and
wholesale distributors.

