TeamLinks Office V2.5 for Windows and Other TeamLinks Enhancements

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Mobile computing release with new international spell checker

o  VTX server now supports OpenVMS Alpha systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital's solution to meet the needs of users looking for client/server
groupware applications and user working from remote locations and while
traveling is TeamLinks Office V2.5 for Windows client and the TeamLinks
Office Server V2.5. TeamLinks Office for Windows has added many new features
that make working while disconnected from the server easier than ever. All
five TeamLinks applications (Mail, Routing, Conferencing, Library Services,
and Calendar Manager) now support a new easy-to-use remote connection
capability. In addition, new features in the conferencing and library
services clients improve the integration with the TeamLinks Office suite.

DEC VTX V6.2 server has also been enhanced by adding OpenVMS Alpha system
support. Furthermore, with ALL-IN-1 software as the mail server, users can
have all five TeamLinks Office application servers (ALL-IN-1, TeamRoute for
ALL-IN-1, Notes, DEC VTX, and Calendar Manager) on the Alpha platform for a
complete solution.

TeamLinks Product Enhancements

o  TeamLinks Office V2.5 for Windows (SPD 63.25)
   - A new modem broker provides seamless connections from the TeamLinks
     suite of applications to the backend servers (e.g. File Cabinet, Mail,
     Routing, Notes, VTX, and Calendar Manager).
   - A streamlined TeamLinks Office common install procedure reduces the
     installation time of all five client applications.
   - V2.5 offers support for IBM's OS/2 platform using the WIN-OS/2
     environment.
   - A CD-ROM packaging option for the TeamLinks Office for Windows client
     (SPD 63.25.01) is now available.

o  TeamLinks Mail and Routing V2.5 for Windows
   - Offline mode allows a user to work without any connection to a mail
     server.
   - Script editor enables simple client-based filtering, and allows the
     automation of copying, moving, and sending of documents between server
     and client file cabinets.
   - International spell checker allows users to check spelling in the
     create message window.

o  TeamLinks Conferencing V2.5 for Windows (SPD 38.65)
   - Improved TeamLinks Office Integration includes the ability to choose
     TeamLinks environment as default through Preferences option, and the
     ability to extract Notes data to the TeamLinks file cabinet and import
     TeamLinks data into Notes conferences
   - Improved user interface includes the ability to select small buttons
     option for the button bar display, an improved Customize Button Bar
     Dialog box that enhances the users ability to customize the
     look-and-feel of the Conferencing client, and removal of the interim
     mail dialog box, which now allows TeamLinks Mail dialog box to directly
     appear

o  TeamLinks Library Services V2.5 for Windows (SPD 52.62)
   - Improved TeamLinks Office integration includes the ability to export or
     extract a VTX page to the TeamLinks File Cabinet.
   - Mastersoft viewers are now included and may be installed optionally..
   - A connect dialog allows a list of frequently accessed servers or pages
     (via keywords) to be selected and defined with ease.
   - Improved mail integration makes it easier for a user to mail launchable
     pages (requires TeamLinks Office for non-text pages).
   - There is improved document handling with a new associations dialog

o  DEC VTX V6.2 for OpenVMS VAX (SPD 26.57) and Alpha systems (SPD 64.05.00)
   - Alpha support and enhancements to the search capabilities of the text
     retrieval search engine have been added.
   - A new /TIMEOUT qualifier has been added to the OPEN/INDEX command in
     VTX CTL.
   - The PRINT ALL and SAVE ALL commands are now fixed customizable via
     VTX.INI.
   - Support for Dutch language has been added in VTX ACU.
   - There have been many software fixes since V6.0.

BENEFITS

o  TeamLinks is now easier to order, install, and use, particularly when in
   a mobile or remote situation.
o  TeamLinks Office server with ALL-IN-1 now delivers a complete Alpha
   system solution.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

TeamLinks Office V2.5 will be available June 1995.

