DECswitch 400 Ethernet/ATM Switch

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Ethernet/ATM switch for connecting Ethernet stations to 155 Mb per second
   ATM backbones over multimode fiber

o  Up to 24 10BaseT Ethernet ports

o  AUI, ThinWire, and multimode fiber optic Ethernet ports supported

o  Virtual LAN capability

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DECswitch 400 system is an Ethernet/ATM switch suited for connecting
Ethernet stations to ATM backbones. The initial product supports up to 24
10BaseT Ethernet ports. Ethernet modules to support AUI, multimode fiber,
and ThinWire Ethernet also are available.

The DECswitch 400 is packaged in a five slot, 19-inch rackmountable chassis.
The chassis includes a management module, power supply, and rackmounting
brackets. Line cards are purchased separately and installed by the user.
Either single or dual port OC3 (155 Mb per second over multimode fiber with
SONET/SDH framing) ATM interfaces are available.

Permanent Virtual Circuits (PVCs) and Switched Virtual Circuits (SVCs) are
supported, as are Constant Bit Rate (CBR), Variable Bit Rate (VBR), and
Available Bit Rate (ABR) traffic classes. Virtual LANs are supported with
the ability to route between virtual LANs via IP. IPX routing is planned.

A DECswitch 400 switch can be managed by any SNMP compliant network
management application. The DECswitch 400 switch may also be managed through
an out-of-band management interface via Serial Line Internet Protocol
(SLIP).

The DECswitch 400 is not a DEChub product.

BENEFITS

o  High performance connectivity from Ethernet to ATM or Ethernet to
   Ethernet is provided via personal Ethernet connections.

o  Ability to segment workgroups into virtual LANs, enabling separation of
   workgroups, ease of management of the workgroups, and ease of mobility of
   workgroup members.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECswitch 400 system will be available in June 1995 through Digital and
its value-added resellers (bundled with implementation services or
application-specific solutions), distributors, and integrators. Volume
availability will occur in July 1995.

o  Order a DECswitch 400 chassis (DESSA-AA). The chassis includes a single
   power supply, rackmount brackets, and backup firmware diskette. (The
   firmware is preloaded at the factory.)

o  A management module, DESSR-AA, is required and must be ordered. An
   additional management module may be ordered for redundancy. If the
   primary management module fails, there will be an automatic failover.
   However, an additional chassis slot will be taken for this additional
   management module, thus reducing the maximum number of Ethernet ports.

o  Order one of the ATM line cards as follows:
   - If a single ATM port is needed, order the DESSL-AA.
   - If two ATM ports are needed, order the DESSL-AB.

o  Order Ethernet line cards based on the type of Ethernet interface desired
   and the number of ports needed. The type of interface can be mixed, based
   on the Ethernet line cards used. Up to three Ethernet line cards may be
   placed in a chassis if an ATM line card is installed. Four Ethernet line
   cards may be installed if no ATM line card is installed. The ordering
   information is as follows:

   - DESSL-EA: Eight 10BaseT Ethernet ports per line card
   - DESSL-EB: Six port universal Ethernet line card that requires daughter
     cards dependent on the type of interface desired:

     - DESSM-AA: One AUI and one 10BaseT interface. Up to three may be
       placed on a single DESSL-EB.
     - DESSM-AB: One 10BaseT interface. Up to six may be placed on a single
       DESSL-EB.
     - DESSM-AC: One multimode fiber optic interface with ST connector. Up
       to six may be placed on a single DESSL-EB.
     - DESSM-AD: One ThinWire interface with BNC connector. Up to six may be
       placed on a single DESSL-EB. Daughter cards may be mixed on a
       DESSL-EB line card.

o  The user's manual (EK-DESSA-UG) needs to be ordered separately.

o  Order a redundant power supply, DESSP-AA, if desired.

o  Order the power cord for each DESSP-AA for non-U.S. versions. (The power
   cord for the U.S. model is included with the power supply for the U.S.
   version.)

o  LAN emulation client software is planned. Network management system
   software for MS-DOS with Windows will be available in September 1995 for
   managing the DECswitch 400 system.

