SERVICES

Users should be strongly encouraged to purchase supplemental services with
this product. These services include unlimited 7 day a week, 24 hours a day
access to toll-free technical support and information databases, access to
the latest firmware, troubleshooting, and onsite repair of the DECswitch
400. Users can select an onsite service level -- from next-day onsite to 7
day a week, 24 hours a day committed onsite within 4 hours.

While the product is under warranty, supplemental services are available at
reduced rates.

Other service levels and multi-year agreements are also available. Under
product warranty, users are required to isolate problems to the failing
field replaceable unit (FRU), call Digital to receive a Return Authorization
(RA) number, mail the failed FRU to Digital, and install the replacement FRU
into the DECswitch 400 system. This scenario has an overall problem
resolution time of several days. Warranty without service should only be
offered to users who are technically proficient with the product, require
limited technical support, and do not mind the turnaround time needed to
receive a replacement FRU.

Digital product installation services are available and are recommended.
This price covers installation of the entire system (chassis, power
supplies, line cards, and daughter cards). Installation prices also are
available for options added to the system subsequent to initial install.
Users who are not trained and experienced with the product should have
Digital do the installation. Digital installation will save these users time
and money, as well as increase overall satisfaction with the product.

TECHNICAL DATA

The DECswitch 400 is a five-slot, rackmount chassis. One of the slots is
reserved for management functions. The other four slots are for use by
Ethernet or ATM line cards or an additional, redundant management module.

The DECswitch 400 switch provides high performance (640 Mb per second bus
switch architecture) and low latency. It supports 802.1d Spanning Tree
Transparent Bridging, with 1,000 bridging addresses supported per Ethernet
module. Custom filtering is also supported.

There are two ATM interface modules: a single port and a dual port version.
They provide 155 Mb per second, multimode fiber connections to an ATM
network with SC connectors and use SONET/SDH framing (OC3). The following
ATM features are supported:

o  ATM Forum UNI 3.0 or UNI 3.1
o  PVCs and SVCs
o  Adaptation layers 5 and 3/4
o  ABR and UBR classes of service

There are two Ethernet modules available: an eight-port 10BaseT module with
RJ45 connector and a six-port universal module that requires daughter cards
to provide the physical interface. Four physical interface daughter cards
are available as follows:

o  One daughter card provides one AUI and one 10BaseT interface. Up to three
   of these daughter cards can be connected to a universal Ethernet module
   for a total of three AUI connections and three 10BaseT connections.
o  One daughter card provides one 10BaseT interface. Up to six of these
   daughter cards can be connected to a universal Ethernet module.
o  One daughter card provides one multimode fiber interface with an ST
   connector. Up to six of these daughter cards can be connected to a
   universal Ethernet module.
o  One daughter card provides one ThinWire interface with a BNC connector.
   Up to six of these daughter cards can be connected to a universal
   Ethernet module.

The daughter cards may be mixed on a universal Ethernet card.

The DECswitch 400 switch provides virtual LAN capability. Up to 32 virtual
LANs are supported per switch with up to 65,000 virtual LANs supported per
network. The DECswitch 400 switch provides routing between virtual LANs with
IP routing. Up to 16 IP router ports can be configured with only one IP
router port per VLAN. IPX routing is planned.

The DECswitch 400 switch supports IP protocols RIP, ICMP, UDP, SNMP, TCP,
FTP, TELNET (client only), SLIP, and Rlogin (client and server).

High availability is provided through:

o  Redundant power supply option with dual AC input
o  Redundant fans (standard)
o  Redundant management module option
o  Hot swap capability line cards and power supply
o  Temperature alarm (standard)

The DECswitch 400 switch can be managed by any SNMP-compliant network
management application. SNMP MIBs and agents are provided with the DECswitch
hardware. The switch also can be managed through an out-of-band management
interface via SLIP.

LAN Emulation Client (LEC) per the ATM Forum specification is planned.
FLOWmaster flow control is not supported.

A Token Ring module will be added to the DECswitch 400 in late 1995. This
will enable the DECswitch 400 to provide Token Ring to Ethernet or ATM
switching, enabling users to provide high speed connectivity for the most
common LAN technologies to ATM backbones.

Future updates to the firmware will be downline-loadable.

