Multia X Server Option V3.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  32 bit X11.R6 Server for Multia MultiClient Desktop

o  Performance optimized for Multia hardware

o  Integrated with Multia Configuration Manager for remote setup and control
   of user environment

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Multia X Server Option V3.0 provides access to UNIX and OpenVMS X
applications from Multia Desktops. It is optimized for the Multia platform,
and provides users with the software features and performance they expect
from best in class X terminals.

Features include:

o  XIE (X Image Extension) V3.0 and V5.0.
o  Shape extension -- Supports non-rectangular window. Other X extensions
   include misc, Big_request, xtest, and Record.
o  The ability to create X sessions to networked hosts via DECnet, TCP/IP,
   or LAT.
o  X Display Manager Control Protocol support (XDMCP) for host connections.
o  NFS client support to access file and font services on host systems that
   support TCP/IP and NFS.
o  SaveUnder and Backing Store.
o  Font formats supported include .FON, .BDF, .PCF, Speedo, Type1, and SNF
   fonts as well as font servers. The Multia X Server comes with several
   standard font sets. Access to remote fonts is supported over TCP/IP, DAP,
   NFS, and font servers.
o  Choice of single-window mode (displays all X applications in a single X
   Root window) or multi-window mode (displays each X application in a
   separate X Root window).
o  Local Motif Window Manager. The user can select an alternate remote
   window manager or use the local Windows based window manager.
o  Context sensitive online help.
o  Two-way cut and paste for text.
o  Graphics cut and paste for Windows.
o  Enhanced logging to write server messages to log file, message window, or
   Windows NT events logger.
o  Mouse button 2 emulation.
o  Supports PseudoColor, StaticColor, GrayScale, TrueColor, and StaticGray
   display. Full plane mask support.
o  Security features include user level access control and authorization on
   DECnet.

Full Integration with Multia Base Software

The Multia X Server Option is completely integrated into the Configuration
Manager included in Multia Base Software V3.0. (See the "Multia Base
Software V3.0 and Multia System Administrator Kit V3.0" article in this
issue.) From within the Configuration Manager, the "Customize Multia" window
provides a graphical user interface that enables system administrators to
customize the X environment remotely for one or hundreds of users. For
example, for any workgroup of Multia Desktops in the network, system
administrators can:

o  Enable and disable use of the Multia X Server.
o  Enable and disable advanced display accelerator functions and X
   extensions, such as X Image Extension (XIE).
o  Specify a color scheme for X window controls that differs from the one
   used for Windows applications.
o  Select single-window or multi-window mode.
o  Optimize displays for performance and precision by setting graphic
   display features such as monitor dimensions, X window panning, and
   compatibility with other X11.R3 applications.
o  Define font access and paths.
o  Specify host nodes that can access the Multia X Server. In this way,
   system administrators can control which applications and host can be
   accessed by the end user.
o  Enable and disable XDMCP, and specify the startup method and
   configuration settings for the host system.
o  Set a password for accessing the Multia X Server.
o  With the Multia X Serial Line Protocol option, specify the serial port
   communications settings, direct or modem connection, and configure modem
   settings.

BENEFITS

o  Integration with Multia Configuration Manager simplifies end user access
   to X applications and greatly reduces system administrator setup and
   support time.

o  Performance is optimized for Multia Desktops.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

Both Multia X Server Option and eXcursion V2.0 for Windows NT support
complete X11.R6 server and extensions functionality, plus many additional
features. (See the "eXcursion V2.0 for Windows and Windows NT" article in
this issue.) The products are significantly different in the following ways:

o  eXcursion V2.0 is a standalone, shrink-wrapped software package that can
   be installed on any PC running Windows or Windows NT running on Alpha,
   MIPS, or Intel platforms. Multia X Server software will run only on
   Multia Desktops.

o  The Multia X Server Option has been optimized for the Multia hardware. A
   unique performance driver tunes the Multia X Server to the graphics
   accelerator in the Multia system box. The eXcursion product is not
   optimized for one particular hardware platform.

o  The Multia X Server is completely integrated into the Multia Base
   Software and specifically the Configuration Manager. It can be remotely
   installed on multiple Multia Desktops from a single location. The system
   administrator can remotely configure and customize X Server features, as
   listed above.

o  Multia X Server includes support for the NFS client protocol.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Multia X Server Option V3.0 and Multia X Serial Line Protocol Option are
available now. Media distribution is done through the Multia System
Administrator Kit. Users who have purchased eXcursion V1.2 for Windows NT to
use on Multia Desktops can upgrade to the Multia X Server Option at no
charge.

