Cognos' Axiant V1.1 for Digital UNIX and V1.2 for OpenVMS Alpha

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Axiant is a Windows based graphical development environment for building
   client/server applications that will run on Microsoft Windows, OpenVMS,
   Digital UNIX, and other UNIX based operating systems

o  Applications can be partitioned to take advantage of five different
   deployment topologies: mobile; client with data server; client with
   application server; functionally distributed (mixed); and server only

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Cognos, Inc.'s Axiant is a graphical application development environment
that enables users to create mission-critical client/server applications on
Microsoft Windows based systems, and then run the applications on Windows,
OpenVMS, and UNIX based servers. V1.1 and V1.2 are built upon and add
substantially to the strengths of Cognos' PowerHouse 4GL software, providing
the full three tier client/server capability (see article in the May 1995
issue of Digital's Customer Update). Axiant V1.0 works with multiple
databases on multiple platforms, and provides the Impromptu and PowerPlay
reporting tools to deliver a single, proven deployment environment.

BENEFITS

Axiant V1.1 and V1.2 support the automatic development of client/server
applications that meet a wide range of needs, such as traditional
transaction processing and easy graphical access to corporate information.
Applications built with Axiant software can leverage the power of clients
and servers, as well as work against multiple databases and platforms. The
Impromptu tool provides ad hoc query and reporting capabilities that allow
end users to query data sources by clicking on a tool bar in a single,
unified graphical environment. The PowerPlay tool enables users to explore,
analyze, and report on complex multi-dimensional data. Together, Axiant,
Impromptu, and PowerPlay software enable developers to build applications
with both data processing and end-user information components.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Axiant V1.1 and V1.2 are available now through your local Cognos office. The
price, based on the number of users, begins at $3,000.

SERVICES

Cognos provides service, training, user support, and consulting.

