Exide Powerware Series-PLUS 8 kVA thru 36 kVA UPS Pricing Reduced

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Reduced prices on 8 kVA through 36 kVA models

o  Maximum uptime solutions for critical systems and greater customer
   satisfaction at up to 13 percent savings

o  Industry leading technology provides competitive price/performance with
   service plans unmatched by the competition

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Powerware Series-PLUS is an industry leading true online Uninterruptible
Power System (UPS) that utilizes a state-of-the-art high frequency inverter
design. This design provides a more compact, efficient, and quieter solution
for any business environment. Models are available in 8 kVA thru 12kVA
single-phase and 15 kVA through 36 kVA three-phase output. These systems are
intended to protect critical computing and networking applications that
require continuous access during any power anomaly. The products satisfy
power protection needs for most midrange systems, telecommunications,
networking, and multiple workstation environments.

Digital has reduced the price on all Exide Powerware-Series PLUS models from
8kVA to 36 kVA. The 8 kVA through 18kVA models readily accept 176 to 256
volts input with selectable output voltage. They feature an optional power
distribution module with choice of both 120V and 240V output receptacle
configurations.

Applications

The 8, 10, and 12kVA single phase models are well suited for VAX 7000 and
DEC 7000 rackmounts and the new AlphaServer 8200 and 8400 one-phase systems
using multiple expansion cabinets. The 15 kVA or 18kVA three-phase models
are ideal for VAX 7000 and DEC 7000 and the new three-phase AlphaServer 8200
and 8400 applications.

The 24 kVA and 36kVA models feature an optional power distribution cabinet,
with provisions for up to 30 Square D circuit breakers, and an accessory
options cabinet with a full wraparound maintenance bypass switch and choice
of input THD reduction filter or a 480V to 208/240V step-down transformer.

BENEFITS

PowerWare Series-PLUS UPS ensures that business operations remain unaffected
by all power abnormalities by providing:

o  Total power protection and battery backup -- Allows computer and
   communications systems to continue operation, regardless of the state of
   power.

o  True online technology -- Inverter carries 100 percent load continuously
   for rock solid voltage and frequency output, regardless of the state of
   the incoming power. This is ideal for generator applications where
   frequency varies widely.

o  Improved system reliability -- There is a more robust online inverter
   design with the load not dependent on a single switch. This eliminates
   last minute surprises associated with equipment degradation over time.

o  Computer grade design -- Designed to fully support nonlinear loads
   without derating, it provides highest reliability as components are
   properly sized in the design.

o  Investment protection -- There is upgradeability from 8 kVA to 12kVA, 15
   kVA to 18kVA, and 24 kVA to 36kVA, and expandability to increase battery
   support time.

o  Communications for network power management -- Power management software
   provides continuous monitoring for safe, unattended system shutdown and
   system diagnostics. Also provided is a network monitoring interface via
   SNMP or network adaptors. RS232 also allows two-way communication between
   the UPS and any terminal.

o  Compatible with Digital's exclusive VAX and Alpha remote environmental
   monitoring software (REMS) -- This provides for lights-out operation.

o  Feature-rich -- Features include an LCD front panel display, programmable
   parameters, 33 customized relay output settings, EPO/REPO interface, and
   seismic anchors or castors standard.

o  Maximum uptime with static and maintenance bypass -- Static bypass
   automatically transfers the critical load to utility power during an
   overload condition or system fault, and allows it to remain online during
   the worst of conditions. Transfer back to inverter power is also fully
   automatic. Maintenance bypass provides transparent transfer of CPU to
   utility power during routine maintenance.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Powerware Series-PLUS UPS systems are available through Digital, the
DECdirect service, Business Recovery Services Sales, and Digital's business
partners. Consult the February 1995 edition of Digital's Systems and Options
Catalog for configuration and ordering information, including network
connectivity options and UPS monitoring software.

The system is delivered in sections -- the UPS cabinet, the battery
cabinet(s), and the distribution module, which are attached at the time of
installation. The electrical input and output are hardwired as the standard
configuration. The optional power distribution module allows direct plug-in
output connection on 8 kVA through 18 kVA models. Flexible power cables with
attached circuit breakers and receptacles are available for the 24 kVA
through 36 kVA models.

