eXcursion V2.0 for Windows and Windows NT

HIGHLIGHTS

o  32 bit X11.R6 PC X server

o  PC X server performance at X terminal speeds

o  eXcursion Remote Access supports X access over serial lines

o  Best-in-class ease of use with new "Windows 95 look and feel" user
   interface

o  Localized for eight European languages plus Hebrew character support

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

eXcursion V2.0 is a next-generation PC X server product for Microsoft
Windows and Windows NT desktops. It enables X-based applications running on
remote host systems to be displayed alongside Windows applications on
Windows or Windows NT desktops. This new version offers the performance of
the industry's leading PC X servers, providing a stable, dependable
environment for demanding, graphics-intensive X application displays. Users
can run X application sessions side by side with popular Windows
applications -- and even cut and paste text and graphics between
heterogeneous applications.

X Access Without Compromise

V2.0 is based on the latest version of the X Window System, X11.R6, an
industry standard model for developing and running client/server
applications. Compliance with X11.R6 includes support of X extensions, font
transformations, and improved graphics, enabling users to display the most
advanced X applications.

X terminal class performance equals that of industry-leading PC X servers,
providing uncompromised performance when displaying graphics-intensive
applications.

A completely redesigned user interface incorporates best-in-class ease of
use with a "Windows 95 look and feel" tabbed folder design control panel.
The new user interface makes eXcursion V2.0 even easier to configure and
use.

eXcursion Remote Access

eXcursion Remote Access uses NCD's XRemote protocol to enable PCs running
eXcursion to communicate over serial lines (such as telephone lines) with
higher performance than protocols such as Serial Line Internet Protocol
(SLIP) or Point to Point Protocol (PPP). Remote Access provides a fully
functional X environment and the convenience of dialing in from a remote
location.

The eXcursion kit includes the startup files required to use X applications
on the following host systems:

o  Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1)
o  ULTRIX
o  OpenVMS Alpha and VAX
o  IBM AIX
o  HP-UX
o  Sun

Local Language Support

eXcursion V2.0 supports the following European languages:

o  French
o  Finnish
o  German
o  Italian
o  Spanish
o  Swedish
o  Danish

The eXcursion user interface, online help, and other messages can be
displayed in any of these languages. Localized, shrinkwrapped kits with
translated documentation will be available in Europe.

Support for Hebrew applications is also available. A Hebrew kit, which
contains Hebrew fonts on diskettes for eXcursion for Windows software, is
available in Europe. (All eXcursion for Windows NT kits include the Hebrew
fonts on the eXcursion CD-ROM.)

SERVICES

Twelve months of Digital telephone support is included with every eXcursion
license purchased.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

eXcursion for Windows NT V2.0 is now available. eXcursion for Windows V2.0
will be available in July 1995. The eXcursion Software Developer Kit for
Windows NT V2.0 will be available in August 1995. Localized versions of
eXcursion for Windows NT V2.0 will be available in June 1995. Localized
versions of eXcursion for Windows V2.0 will be available in JUly 1995.

eXcursion for Windows NT V2.0 is available as a CD-ROM only kit. Diskettes
for installing eXcursion for Windows NT on Intel systems (English only) are
available by sending in the "If You Need Diskettes" card enclosed in
eXcursion for Windows NT shrinkwrapped kits. In future releases, eXcursion
for Windows NT will be available exclusively on CD-ROM. eXcursion for
Windows V2.0 is available as a CD-ROM kit, as well as the traditional RX23
kit.

