Multia Base Software V3.0 and Multia System Administrator Kit V3.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Supports DECnet and LAT protocols

o  Remote Maintenance Facility simplifies software updates

o  Configuration Manager integrates new Multia software options

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Multia MultiClient Desktop is a network-ready desktop device that lets
users run PC, UNIX, VMS, and mainframe applications simultaneously over
industry standard network protocols. Multia Base Software is pre-installed
on each Multia MultiClient Desktop configuration. (See the "Multia Family of
MultiClient Desktops" article in the December 1994 Digital's Customer Update
for a complete description.)

Multia Base Software V3.0

Multia Base Software V3.0 supports the following new features:

o  DECNET -- Users can create X sessions via DECnet using the Multia X
   Server Option. In a PATHWORKS environment, users can connect to PATHWORKS
   servers for print and file services. A PATHWORKS client license must be
   purchased in order to connect to a PATHWORKS environment. DECnet
   information can now be accessed from the Multia STATUS application.

o  LAT service classes -- LAT service classes 1, 3, and 4 are supported for
   creating terminal sessions, X sessions (with the Multia X Server Option),
   and font access from Multia.

o  Remote STATUS support -- System administrators can obtain Multia
   configuration details remotely (e.g., memory installed, DECnet and TCP/IP
   addresses, software versions, available option, or which applications are
   being run or accessed by the end user).

o  Enhanced Configuration Manager -- The Configuration Manager now enables
   Multia software options to be installed remotely. Software options can be
   installed from the Multia System Administrator Kit to one or many Multia
   Desktops on the network. In addition, system administrators can remotely
   configure and lock user settings for the Multia X Server Option. (See the
   "Multia X Server Option V3.0" article in this issue.)

Each Multia Desktop configuration includes a single user license for the
Multia Base Software. Existing users should purchase the Multia V2.5 to V3.0
upgrade license. (See the AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING section in this article
for full details.)

Multia System Administrator Kit

The Multia System Administrator Kit V3.0 provides additional tools for the
system administrator. One kit is a prerequisite for each Multia
installation. This kit includes CD-ROM media containing Multia Software for
System Administrators and a single user license, plus hardcopy Multia System
Administrator information and installation instructions. Additional users of
the Multia software options will need to purchase the appropriate software
option license per seat. It also includes 90-day telephone support for
software. After the 90-day period, ongoing telephone support can be
purchased from Digital.

The Multia Software for System Administrators includes:

o  Backup copy of Multia Base Software V3.0.
o  All Multia software options (X Server and RUMBA for Mainframe for Multia)
   with single user license.
o  Additional software features for the system administrator, including:
   - Remote Maintenance Facility, which enables a system administrator to
     easily schedule updates to multiple Multia Desktops from a central
     location. Updates can include software, such as new versions of Multia
     software, options, or operating systems; new Multia firmware updates;
     restoring Multia software to a corrupted desktop; or support files for
     X and NFS connections on a host system.
   - Host kits for backup and support of Multia software on Windows NT
     servers, UNIX, and VMS host systems.
   - Configuration templates for creating workgroups.

BENEFITS

o  The ability to access multiple application types simultaneously improves
   user productivity through multitasking.

o  Central desktop management simplifies the user environment and results in
   a lower cost of operation compared to PCs or workstations.

o  Interoperability features, such as embedded network protocols, UNIX,
   OpenVMS, PC, and legacy application access provide seamless access to
   multiple networks and applications. Users do not need to change existing
   environments in order to provide users with access to a wide variety of
   applications across the network.

o  Superior ease of use via the combination of Configuration Manager and
   Application Manager lowers the cost of training and supporting end users.

o  The performance of Alpha technology brings users optimal performance on
   the desktop for accessing multiple application types simultaneously.

o  The Multia MultiClient Desktop system provides a more secure environment
   than networked PCs.

