StorageWorks HSD10 DSSI to SCSI-2 Array Controller

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Offers 100 percent performance improvement over HSD05

o  Provides a non-redundant connectivity for up to 7 SCSI devices, with up
   to 32 MB of read cache in a 3-1/2-inch StorageWorks System Building Block

o  Onboard RAID 0 (striping) standard

o  Allows HSD10 controllers to be warm-swapped for high availability

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The StorageWorks HSD10 Array Controller brings improved DSSI support to the
StorageWorks family of products. The HSD10 connects to a single port on the
DSSI bus providing connectivity for up to seven non-redundant SCSI devices.
The HSD10 allows users the flexibility to expand the amount of
DSSI-connected storage devices or to free up DSSI nodes for host
connections. It supports warm-swapping of the controller and provides
controller based striping (RAID 0) as a feature for improved performance.
The performance of the HSD10, providing 1,000 I/O requests per second, is a
100 percent improvement over the HSD05. The inclusion of 16 or 32 MB of read
cache can reduce response times substantially.

The HSD10 is housed in a 3-1/2-inch StorageWorks form factor system
buildiing block (SBB) and mounts in a BA350-SA shelf along with up to six
SCSI devices. Up to seven HSD10 array controllers may be daisy chained
together utilizing the tri-link connector to fully utilize the DSSI bus. The
tri-link connector and a bus terminator are shipped as part of the HSD10.
The maximum DSSI bus length is 60 feet utilizing the HSD10.

BENEFITS

Many users are reaching storage capacity limitations on their DSSI systems
and clusters, causing them to require additional device connectivity. To
meet these needs, the HSD10 offers:
o  Expanded DSSI connectivity
o  Industry standard SCSI devices
o  Ease of migration to other DSSI environments
o  Direct connection to the DSSI bus
o  Connection for up to seven non-redundant SCSI devices, (Only six SCSI
   devices can be configured in the StorageWorks Shelf with the HSD10)
o  Attached disks may be warm-swapped
o  Provides controller based RAID 0 (striping)
o  Multihost operation, up to four hosts on the DSSI bus
o  Up to 1,000 I/O requests per second and 3 MB per second
o  Controller warm-swap
o  Up to 32 MB of read cache
o  Future availability of optional RAID 1 (mirroring)
o  Connection to a VCS console via a RS communications port

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The StorageWorks HSD10 Array Controller is available now.

The HSD10 will replace the HSD05 DSSI Array Controller. The last order date
for the HSD05 June 1995.

