TECHNICAL DATA

o  Supported SCSI devices:
   - RZ26, RZ26L, RZ28, RZ28B, RZ28D, RZ29B, RZ73, and RZ74
   - EZ51R and EZ54R
   - TLZ06, TLZ6L, TLZ07, TLZ7L, TZ86, and TZ87,
   - RRD43 and RRD44
   - RWZ52

o  Supported adapters:
   - EDA670 VAX 4000 Internal DSSI Adapter
   - D4000 DEC 4000 Internal DSSI Adapter
   - KFDDA and KFDDB VAX 4000 DSSI Option
   - KFMSA VAX 7000/10000 XMI to DSSI Adapter
   - KFQSA MV3 XXX/VAX 4000 QBUS to DSSI Adapter
   - KFESA DEC 2000/2100 EISA to DSSI Adapter

o  Supported StorageWorks environments and cabinets:
   - BA350-SB, BA350-JA, BA350-KA, and BA350-LA
   - SW500-AC/AD and SW800-AA/AB

o  Supported operating systems:
   - OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2 and later
   - Open VMS Alpha V6.1 and later

o  Supported device and option capabilities:
   - Up to seven non-redundant disk storage devices on same SCSI bus from
     the HSD10
   - Up to two tape storage devices on same SCSI bus from HSD10
   - Two solid-state storage device on a SCSI bus from HSD10
   - Up to two tape and two disk or one tape and five disk devices on a SCSI
     bus from HSD10

o  Unsupported device and option capabilities:
   - Combined use of HSD10 and DWZZA adapters

o  For optimal performance it is recommended that the HSD10 be operated at a
   maximum of 80 percent utilized. This will allow for optimal performance
   with workload peaks. If an HSD10 is more than 80 percent utilized,
   purchase of an additional controller should be considered.

SERVICES

Digital Multivendor Customer Services are available for the HSD10. The HSD10
has a one-year onsite and two-year return to factory warranty.



