Alpha/UPS Campaign Delivers Free UPS Monitoring Software

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Special limited time offer for Alpha users in the U.S., Canada, Mexico,
   and most Caribbean islands

o  Free power management software with purchase of Prestige 650-6000va or
   Powerware Series 2000 desktop UPS

o  Exclusive three year hot swap warranty with next day delivery

o  Prestige awarded "best-in-class" technology of 11 top vendors tested by
   LAN Magazine

DESCRIPTION

Until September 30th, Digital is offering Alpha users the opportunity to
obtain the benefits of application preservation and network power management
for free when they purchase premium online power protection.

All AlphaServer system shipments now include a direct marketing brochure
with a coupon that entitles Alpha users to free UPS power management
software -- a $189 to $299 value -- with each purchase of a Powerware
Prestige or Personal 2000 Uninterruptable Power System (UPS). The Prestige
family represents award winning technology that was recognized as "best in
class" in a recent issue of LAN Magazine.

This special Digital offer will be packaged with most AlphaStation
workstation shipments by the end of May.

BENEFITS

Coupling UPS power monitoring software with industry leading UPS technology
offers a total level of protection for Alpha systems and applications,
making the monitoring software a critical and necessary component to any UPS
application.

Powerware UPS systems offer:

o  Upgradeable, extendible features on select models.
o  Proven performance on Digital's leading systems.
o  Full interoperability of software on most major platforms.
o  Exclusive cell saver design with widest voltage window and increased
   battery life.
o  Automatic self battery test.
o  Energy Star and ISO9001 compliance.
o  $25,000 Powerware Protection Guarantee to ensure performance.
o  Reduced life-cycle costs with hot swap bypass option.
o  Digital's exclusive three-year hot swap warranty with next-day
   turnaround.

When used with power management software, a UPS ensures:

o  Graceful system shutdown and cache memory transfer protection during
   power loss.
o  Continuous and distributed monitoring of all UPS across the enterprise.
o  A money-saving alternative to network redundancy.
o  Energy savings from "off and reboot" control during idle hours.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

To simplify the UPS ordering process, the brochure enclosed with each system
provides a cross-reference chart that matches the appropriate UPS system to
each Alpha product (a copy is included in this article). This brochure also
features technical specifications, pictures, and the LAN Magazine
testimonial to help the user make an informed decision. Once the UPS order
is placed, a faxback coupon allows the users to take advantage of the free
software offering.

